to be unified as one.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.453
And if it works that we get to have kids,

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.900
biologically, that's awesome.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.733
- That's a plus.

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:44.270
- But guess what, there's
other ways to have kids.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.103
- Yeah.

00:06:45.103 --> 00:06:48.234
- For us, adoption was an
avenue for us to have kids.

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:49.067
- [Tristan] Yeah.

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:51.383
- Foster care is an avenue
for people to have children.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:52.630
- Obviously great to meet you.

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:53.483
- [Phil] Thank you.

00:06:53.483 --> 00:06:55.180
- Thank you for just still
being to strong and powerful,

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.013
- [Phil] Thank you.

00:06:56.013 --> 00:06:56.846
- and open.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.100
For me, it's really big to see a man

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.050
be open about this
shortcoming with other men.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:03.670
So this has been a beautiful,
beautiful experience.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.330
- Well I'd say, for you man,

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:06.990
thank you for allowing me to be apart.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:07.823
- For sure.

00:07:07.823 --> 00:07:09.966
- And vulnerability is the
biggest sign of strength I think.

00:07:09.966 --> 00:07:10.799
- For sure.

00:07:10.799 --> 00:07:12.120
- And this generation needs to see it

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.650
because we've gotta get
